WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.460
Five Nights at Freddy's is an accidental phenomenon
the likes of which the world has never known.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.240
Since the first game's release in 2014, the
hit horror series has become a gaming sensation

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.009
that's spawned sequels, a spinoff, tie-in
toys, multiple novels, and now, thanks to

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:19.190
Blumhouse Productions and writer-director
Chris Columbus, a feature film.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:22.920
With a track record that includes Gremlins
and The Goonies, the filmmaker sounds like

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.950
a perfect fit for the series' twisted brand
of horror-comedy.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.610
All the elements for a great horror flick
are there; they just have to be used right.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.470
Here are all the things we're hoping to see
in Five Nights at Freddy's.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.550
Light of the morning

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.820
While the details are always different, each
Five Nights at Freddy's game boils down to

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.910
one goal, surviving the night.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.070
Whether it's a lonely late shift security
guard or a terrified kid in their bedroom,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.370
each game's protagonist is stuck having to
do everything they can to bat back the monsters

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.370
hunting them.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.749
Their only salvation?

00:00:51.749 --> 00:00:52.860
Six AM.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.960
Many of the game's most white-knuckle moments
come in the last stretch of each level before

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.760
morning, after all your resources have been
exhausted and the only thing that can save

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.760
you is the clock.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.560
So, obviously, the movie would do well to
follow the same rules.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.969
A harried hero in a horrid situation, pushed
to the edge of being slaughtered by monsters

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:11.200
which become harmless at the first glimpse
of morning?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.940
A helpless hero getting saved by the clock
will go a long way toward making the movie

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.900
feel like the game, especially if we get a
few of the best scares right near the end

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.740
of 5 AM.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.720
For Five Nights at Freddy's fans, the voice
of the "Phone Guy" is an essential part of

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.520
the Fazbear experience.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:41.740
"Upon discovering a damage or death has occurred,
a missing person report will be filed within

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.500
90 days or as soon as property and premises
have been thoroughly cleaned and bleached."

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.630
Cleverly blending exposition with instruction,
the Phone Guy's messages set the tone for

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.070
each night with chipper yet ominous warnings
about the player's duties, creating a sense

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.149
of isolation that shouldn't be discarded in
the translation to film.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.530
"These characters, if they happen to see you
after hours, probably won't recognize you

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:08.090
as a person, they'll most likely see you as
a metal endoskeleton without its costume on."

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.069
It's pretty much a no-brainer to include Phone
Guy for spooling out the series' weird lore,

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:14.500
and
would also be perfect for a cameo appearance

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.319
from the games' developer and original Phone
Guy voice, Scott Cawthon.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:21.810
Hearing a tired Cawthon on the other end of
the line would be a nice nod to the man who

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.200
laid the foundation for a phenomenon.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.720
"So remember, these characters hold a special
place in the hearts of children, and we need

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:30.580
to show them a little respect.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.580
Okay?"

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.040
Foxy and friends

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.470
It almost goes without saying that a Five
Nights at Freddy's movie isn't going to work

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.580
unless Freddy brings the whole crew.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.440
Inspired by the real-life arcade-and-animatronics
pizza franchise Chuck E. Cheese's, the Five

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.400
Nights at Freddy's series includes a whole
extended family of animatronic entertainers,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.290
and the movie would do well to invite them
all.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.959
Something jumping out of the dark and grabbing
you can get old, so the series' animatronics

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:56.770
all have different attributes.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:01.599
In the Chucky-esque creepy child category,
there's Balloon Boy, and the wholesome-yet-homicidal

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:02.599
Baby.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:07.480
For eerie, haunted circus ambience, there's
the dancing Ballora and the clownish Marionette.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.340
The fleet-footed Foxy and the unsettlingly
toothy Chica are as menacing as any slasher

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.340
villain.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.000
All of these characters bring a different
scary skillset to the table, especially if

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.680
they get the chance, a la Five Nights 4, to
go into nightmare mode.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.140
Put a quarter up

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.910
One of the least-talked about aspects of the
Five Nights series is the stuff that goes

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.659
down between the levels.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:40.010
Since the first entry, the series has featured
little interludes of simple, Atari-style minigames,

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.459
most of which seem pretty normal on the surface.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.709
The happy vibe of the minigames stands in
stark contrast to the pitch-black horror of

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:51.379
the main game, and also set up scares of their
own when the games take turns that are unexpectedly

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:52.400
grim.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.140
Haunted video games have often been the stuff
of crappy creepypasta, but they could serve

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.349
a purpose in the Five Nights movie, especially
if the film is set in an arcade that's open

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:01.480
for business.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:05.980
It's against the series' rules to have animatronics
stalk the halls during business hours, so

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:10.129
having the cloying kids' games take subtle,
dark twists could be a great way to unsettle

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:11.860
an audience in the early going.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:15.660
It's important to know that at Freddy Fazbear's,
a "game over" really means something.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.180
Home delivery

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.711
Five Nights at Freddy's 4 moved the action
from a pizzeria to the bedroom of one of the

00:04:28.711 --> 00:04:32.970
franchise's little guests, making it, by far,
the scariest entry in the series, with the

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:37.690
monster designs going above and beyond the
rest of the games in terms of sheer horror.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:42.310
While the red light-green light gameplay remained
the same, the sense of violation the monsters

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.280
caused went to a whole new level.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.690
It's bad enough to eviscerate kids at the
arcade, but hunting them down in their bedrooms?

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:54.120
That's just terrifying, and if it's done right,
could make for the movie's most sinister scenes.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.350
It's me

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.180
The series' biggest scares can come from the
stuff you don't see coming.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.500
One of the game's more unpredictable elements
is Golden Freddy, a variation on everyone's

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.509
favorite killer bear that will occasionally
appear with no regard to the rules.

00:05:06.509 --> 00:05:10.590
If the player doesn't shake him off in time,
the game itself crashes and resets.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.449
The effect is truly unsettling.

00:05:12.449 --> 00:05:15.990
Kicked out of the game and left staring at
your desktop, you may well feel that the evil

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:17.930
spirits are loose in your computer.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.020
The movie could emulate this by messing with
the fourth wall.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.610
Taking a page out of The Exorcist's book,
the movie could assault the audience with

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.870
subliminal imagery.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:30.759
Or, like in the sequel to Columbus' Gremlins,
the monsters could just burn up the film print,

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.780
breaking out of the movie's world to jump
out of the screen.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.340
The Bite of '87

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.161
If there's one scene that Five Nights fanatics
will be expecting to see in the movie, it's

00:05:49.161 --> 00:05:52.080
probably the infamous "Bite of '87."

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.990
First referenced by the Phone Guy in the first
game, this brutal animatronic attack quickly

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:00.430
became a legendary focal point in Five Nights
at Freddy's lore, serving as the moment Freddy

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:03.410
Fazbear's went from a fun franchise to something
much more evil.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.950
"They used to be allowed to walk around during
the day too, but then there was the Bite of

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:08.950
'87.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:13.410
It's amazing that the human body can live
without the frontal lobe."

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.050
Fans of the series spent months speculating
about the nature of the fateful bite before

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:19.180
the fourth game finally showed it.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.690
Players who reached a certain minigame were
able to watch as a small child's head was

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:27.550
crushed in a pair of animatronic jaws, the
carnage being portrayed in old-school, pixelated

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.550
fashion.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:32.740
If the film brings this to life the right
way, it'll both thrill fans and leave parents

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.850
everywhere wondering how they ever thought
these games were safe for kids.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:37.850
Thanks for watching!

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.990
